/* Explore Database, Versions 6.0 & up */
/* Initial Coding 07/12/80 by Jim Lippard */

/* Long Descriptions */
outside
You are at the edge of a small clearing, surrounded by forest.
To the south is a small wooden shack on the hillside.
end;
shack
You are standing in the center of a small wooden building. Apparently
it was once used as a storage shack for mining tools, for there are
hooks on the walls, but all are empty now. The floor is covered with
dust, and it appears that no one has been here for some time. There
are several windows which let in a small amount of light, and some
empty shelves on the walls. There is a door in the north wall, and
a small trapdoor in the floor.
end;
forest
You are in the forest.
end;
cellar
You are in the cellar of the shack. The walls are composed of a sparkling
rough stone. There is a trapdoor in the ceiling and an opening to the east.
end;
granite
You are in a cave chamber with walls of granite. Passages lead
north, south, and west.
end;
phosphorescent
You are in a glowing cave chamber filled with phosphorescent rocks.
Passages lead north and south.
end;
library
You are in a library. The walls are lined with shelves containing many
books, with titles such as "Creatures of the Past", "The Mystery of the
Moaning Cave", "Demons, Monsters, and Abodes of the Dead", "The Secret
of the Caves", and many more. Passages lead north and east.
end;
mosquito
You are in a room filled with buzzing mosquitoes. There is a small
pool of stagnant water in the northwest corner of the room. Passages
lead south and east.
end;
gold
You are in a cubical chamber with walls of pure gold. Carved
into one wall is the message "All that glitters in this cave is not
gold". Passages lead east and west.
end;
silver
You are in a cubical chamber with walls of pure silver. Carved
into one wall is the message "All that glitters in this cave is not
silver". Passages lead south and west.
end;
platinum
You are in a cubical chamber with walls of pure platinum. Carved
into one wall is the message "All that glitters in this cave is not
platinum". Passages lead north and south.
end;
power
You are in a room with walls of soft earth. Running across the walls
are bare electrical wires. Floating in the center of the room in
midair, unattached to walls or ceiling, is an electrical receptacle.
Passages lead north and west.
end;
weapon
You are in a room whose walls are lined with glass cases filled
with assorted weapons. There is a sign on the wall, lettered in
red block letters, which reads "No Smoking - By Order of the
Explorer Grandmaster". Passages lead south and east.
end;
weapon2
You are in a room whose walls are lined with metal stands
supporting battle axes, spears, lances, and javelins. All are
locked in place. A single spear compartment is empty. Passages
lead north and east.
end;
heated
You are in a heated room with glowing red walls. Passages lead
east and west.
end;
grafitti
You are in a room with walls of slate. They are covered with
grafitti, presumably put there by visitors to the cave. Passages
lead east and west.
end;
elbow
You are in Elbow Pipe, a steel tunnel. There is a single strip of
red carpet down the center of the tunnel to walk upon. Passages
lead south and west.
end;
torches
You are in a fairly long corridor lit by torches lining the walls.
Passages lead north and south.
end;
sand
You are in a room with a small sandy beach to one side. The beach
lines a pond of water, filled by a subterranean spring which
bubbles water up on the far side of the pond. Passages exit to
the north and south.
end;
elbow2
You are in Elbow Pipe II, a steel tunnel. Down the center of the
tunnel is a green carpet for walking upon. Passages lead north
and west.
end;
sorcerer
You are in the Hall of the Sorcerer. The walls are paneled wood,
and the walls are lined with red velvet curtains. Passages exit
to the north and south.
end;
lower-cross
You are in the lower cross room. The walls are made of rough,
unsanded wood. Passages lead north and south.
end;
auxiliary
You are in the Explore Auxiliary Control Center. Along
one wall are disk drives (and several tape drives), along
the other are 4 CPUs, an IOM, DATANET, and 6 SCUs (not to
mention 2M words of main memory. There is also an operator's console
nearby. A passage exits to the west.
end;
crossroads
You are at the Crossroads. Passages lead north, south, east, west, and
down.
end;
brink
You are at the brink of a 1000-foot deep abyss. A dim passage
is visible across the hole on the other side. A passage exits to the
east.
end;
abyss
You are on the west side of the abyss. A single passage leads east
10 feet, and then promptly turns straight down into the abyss.
end;
tunnel1
You are in a complex circuitry of tunnels.
end;
tunnel2
You are in a complex circuitry of tunnels.
end;
tunnel3
You are in a complex circuitry of tunnels.
end;
tunnel4
You are in a complex circuitry of tunnels.
end;
tunnel5
You are in a complex circuitry of tunnels.
end;
tunnel6
You are in a complex circuitry of tunnels.
end;
west-hall
You are at the west end of a long hall stretching out of sight to the
east.
end;
mid-hall
You are at the middle of a long hall stretching out of sight to the
east and west.
end;
east-hall
You are at the east end of a long hall stretching out of sight to the
west.
end;
thin
You are in a very thin room, and
it is difficult to breathe. Passages lead east and west.
end;
dark
You are in an extremely dark room. Your flashlight beam stops
one inch from the end of the flashlight casing, and there seems to be
an evil presence in the room.
end;
waterfall
You are in a chamber with waterfalls on either side. They are
lit from behind by powerful multi-colored spotlights. Passages lead
south and east.
end;
short-hall
You are in a short hall with holes in the ceiling through which sand
is pouring. Passages lead east and west.
end;
elbow3
You are in Elbow Pipe III, a steel tunnel. Passages lead
north and south.
end;
metal
You are in a metal tunnel that leads north and south.
end;
weasel
You are in a cylindrical room with walls and floor covered
with thick, soft fur. Passages lead north, south, east, and
west.
end;
terminal
You are in a room whose walls are lined with VIP7801s, all hardwired
to the Explore Multics. The floor is covered by a soft green carpet.
Passages lead east and west.
end;
Lippard
You are in the Lippard room. Pictures of spotted leopards and black
panthers line the walls. Passages lead east and west.
end;
twisted
You are in a twisted passage. A sign on the wall says "MERLIN".
Passages lead south and east.
end;
chamber
You are in the Chamber of Ages. Ancient sculptures are set on
pedestals around the room. Many glare at you menacingly, appearing
to be almost alive. The base of each statue is labeled with
a gold plaque. One reads:
              Merlin
              Magician
          1159 - ???? A.D.
      "Time/Space Ducts are always nearby"
A passage leads north.
end;
light
You are in a room filled with glaring light from nowhere. It
is very difficult to see. Passages (barely visible) lead south and
west.
end;
experiment
You are in the Explore Experimentation Chamber. Glass cases fill the
room, each containing a small dwarf. As you look closer at one, you
see a card at the end of it which reads "Olney Littlehand".
Passages lead east and west.
end;
basilisk
You are in the basilisk's den. Stone statues of men, looking remarkably
life-like, fill the room. Passages lead north, south, and east.
end;
scroll
You are in a room bare except for a shelf
on one wall, which is covered with papyrus scrolls. Passages lead
south and west.
end;
vault
You are at the entrance to the Vault of Tomorrow. A steel door closes
it off. A passage leads back to the east.
end;
finish
You are in the Vault of Tomorrow. The walls consist of blued steel,
as do the floor and ceiling. Along the top of each wall are several
television screens, each focusing on a different room of the cave. In
in the center of this relatively empty room is a large pedestal, upon
which a figure is seated. A steel plate at the foot of the pedestal
reads "Explorer Grandmaster". The figure rises to his feet, and signals
you to take his place. As he does so, he vanishes into nothingness.
end;
printout-room
You are in a large room, filled with ceiling-high rows of shelves,
each shelf lined with dprints. Passages lead north and south.
end;
edge
You are at the edge of a deep fissure. There is some vegetation here,
along the edge. A dim passage is visible across the fissure.
end;
fissure
You are on the south side of a deep fissure.
end;
no-exits
You are in a small room with no exits. A note on one wall reads
"Remember the magic words".
end;
deadend
You are in a passage which once continued east here, but is now
completely blocked by debris.
end;
limbo
You are in Limbo, where everything goes when it dies. If you
just walked in here, I think it's a bug, so please contact
Lippard.Scouting and report it.
end;
end;

